<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pointe-à-Pitre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pointe-à-Pitre is the largest town and main commercial port of Guadeloupe, on the island of Grande-Terre at the southern end of the channel separating it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basse-terre">Basse-Terre</a>. Developed from the 1760s, it grew into the economic centre of the colony, though the town of Basse-Terre remained the seat of government. It has been rebuilt several times after earthquakes, fires and hurricanes, notably the earthquake of 1843.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pointe-a-pitre.jpg" alt="Pointe-à-Pitre" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zivax · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pointe-%C3%A0-Pitre.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
